: an explicit visible action using the SAME target, such as an applicator touching skin. Wearing clothing, jewelry or makeup alone is insufficient.\nframed_garment_detail: the framing clearly showcases an identifiable cut, finish, fastening or fabric detail of the SAME garment. A visible pattern, face with clothes or full-body view alone is insufficient.\nThe seven presentation configurations require state presented_target and exactly one category. hand_holds_hanger_out, hand_pulls_worn_fabric_out and framed_garment_detail require garment. Other presentation configurations allow cosmetic, applicator, garment or accessory. Cosmetic requires an identifiable cosmetic product; a brush is an applicator, not a cosmetic product, and makeup already worn on a face does not demonstrate a presented product.\nunclear: no presented item is confirmed and a target or its presentation is unclear; state uncertain; categories empty. Ambiguous presentation is uncertain, not incidental_only. A confirmed presented item wins over incidental or ambiguous other items.\nReturn only the JSON object defined by the schema, with every required field exactly once. One configuration and at most one category; no explanations or presentation_cue field. The cue will be a code-derived projection of the declared configuration, not a separate visual observation.",
